      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\n/*\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\n */\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \n * the system.\n */\nvoid body_force(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    float fx = 0.0f; \n    float fy = 0.0f; \n    float fz = 0.0f;\n\n    #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n      float dx = p[j].x - p[i].x;\n      float dy = p[j].y - p[i].y;\n      float dz = p[j].z - p[i].z;\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3; \n      fy += dy * inv_dist3; \n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    p[i].vx += dt*fx; \n    p[i].vy += dt*fy; \n    p[i].vz += dt*fz;\n  }\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\n */\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  /*\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\n   */\n  #pragma omp parallel\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\n    // Force computation with static scheduling (chunk=1) and no barrier after loop\n    #pragma omp for schedule(static,1) nowait\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n      float fx = 0.0f;\n      float fy = 0.0f;\n      float fz = 0.0f;\n\n      #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz)\n      for (int j = 0; j < nbodies; ++j) {\n        float dx = bodies[j].x - bodies[i].x;\n        float dy = bodies[j].y - bodies[i].y;\n        float dz = bodies[j].z - bodies[i].z;\n        float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n        float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n        float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n        fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n        fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n        fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n      }\n\n      bodies[i].vx += DT * fx;\n      bodies[i].vy += DT * fy;\n      bodies[i].vz += DT * fz;\n    }\n\n    // Position update with static scheduling (chunk=1)\n    #pragma omp for schedule(static,1) nowait\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n      bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\n      bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\n      bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\n    }\n\n    // Implicit barrier at end of parallel region ensures all iterations complete before next iter\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(bodies);\n  \n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using a single OpenMP parallel region across all simulation iterations with static scheduling (chunk size 1) for both force computation and position update loops, combined with SIMD reduction on the inner accumulation loop and nowait clauses to eliminate barriers between worksharing constructs within each iteration, reduces synchronization overhead while maintaining load balance through fine-grained work distribution.",
  "notes": "The transformation moves the parallel region outside the iteration loop so that threads are created only once. Inside each iteration, two consecutive #pragma omp for directives with schedule(static,1) distribute bodies evenly among threads; nowait allows threads to proceed immediately from force computation to position update without waiting at a barrier. The inner j-loop uses #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz) to exploit vectorization and reduce scalar overhead. This approach aims to minimize fork-join costs, maximize cache reuse across iterations, and keep all threads busy with fine-grained work items.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Moved parallel region outside the iteration loop (single #pragma omp parallel enclosing all N_ITER iterations)",
    "Added #pragma omp for schedule(static,1) nowait on force computation loop",
    "Added #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz) on inner j-loop within force computation",
    "Added #pragma omp for schedule(static,1) nowait on position update loop"
  ]
